<Layout title="Additional engineering work — Zahin Kabir" active="Projects"><header class="wrap page-top"><a class="back" href={`${base}projects/`}>← All projects</a><p class="eyebrow">EPICS / COMMUNITY DESIGN</p><h1>Food-distribution<br/>bag-filling station</h1><p class="lede">A team project to make filling donated bags easier for volunteers.</p></header><section class="wrap additional-case"><div><p class="eyebrow">07 / EPICS AT PURDUE</p><h2>Food-distribution<br/>bag-filling station</h2><p>Reused donated bags were difficult to hold open while filling. The team explored a bent-wire holder with a bag-tag clip and a bin with hooks, accounting for user height, limited workspace, and the weight of filled bags.</p><p>Both concepts were modeled in SolidWorks and shared with stakeholders for user-preference testing. The final build used two bent-rod bag holders on a cart frame.</p><p class="caption">Designed and built as a team through EPICS at Purdue.</p></div><figure><img src={`${base}assets/epics/bag-station-cad.webp`} alt="Multiple CAD views of the EPICS bag-filling cart and holder concepts" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>SolidWorks concepts for the bag-filling workstation.</figcaption></figure></section></Layout>
